<title>HONG KONG: Taipei top import/export port for HK Jan air cargo.</title>
<headline>Taipei top import/export port for HK Jan air cargo.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taipei remained Hong Kong's leading trading partner for both air cargo imports and exports during January, Civil Aviation Department statistics show.</p>
<p>Reflecting strong trade from south east Asian countries, the amount of air imports from the Thai capital Bangkok continued to increase compared to the previous two months with Singapore, Tokyo-Narita and Seoul in third, fourth and fifth positions respectively.</p>
<p>After Taipei, Singapore and Tokyo Narita were the most popular export ports for Hong Kong goods during January. Frankfurt was the leading European port of entry for Hong Kong goods and New York for the north American market. January 1997 top 20 import ports by scheduled operators to Hong Kong cargo unloaded (in tonnes)</p>
